Third-party code in src/port/aarch64
====================================

This folder holds four files from Arm Optimized Routines, kept byte for byte
as published, with the details below.

libterae's own files here are port_memcpy.S, port_memset.S and
port_memcmp.S. They are under libterae's licence, given at the top of each,
and they only rename the upstream symbols and include the files below. Only
they are assembled: port_memcpy.S gives memcpy and memmove, port_memset.S
gives memset, and port_memcmp.S gives memcmp.

Project:    Arm Optimized Routines
Home:       https://github.com/ARM-software/optimized-routines
Commit:     20859d3fd9e797dde592c489c8ef7d383f778620
Licence:    Each file says "SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0 WITH
            LLVM-exception". libterae takes these files under the MIT
            option, so the licence that applies to them here is MIT. The
            files carry only that identifier, so the MIT text is given in
            full at the end of this file.
Changed:    No. Each file is byte for byte the one at the URL below.

